course: dictionary
lesson: 7636
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the sentence around the word shows you which meaning the writer means. The word product is a good example. «Cleaning products are one of the most common things small children are poisoned by at home.» Here a product is something made to be sold, like a bottle from a shop.
explain: In maths, product means something different. «The product of 3 and 4 is 12.» The product is the answer you get when you multiply numbers. If you see «find the product», you multiply.
explain: In science, a product is a new substance made in a chemical reaction. To choose the right meaning, ask: is this sentence about shops, sums, or results? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A product is something that is made or grown to be sold, such as dairy products or cleaning products.
fact: In maths, the product is the answer when you multiply numbers: the product of 3 and 4 is 12.
fact: A product can also be a result of something, as in «a product of hard work».
fact: In science, a product is a new substance made in a chemical reaction.
fact: «Bleach mixed with some other cleaners gives off a poisonous gas, so cleaning products must never be mixed.»
exercise: «The shop sells dairy products, such as milk and cheese.» What is a product here? | A type of weather | *Something made or grown to be sold | A feeling of hard work | The answer to a sum
exercise: What is the product of 5 and 6? | *30 | 56 | 25 | 11
exercise: «The essay was a product of hard work.» What does product mean here? | A number you multiply | *A result of something | A new substance from a reaction | A bottle from a shop
test: In science, what is a product of a chemical reaction? | A cleaning bottle with a label | The number you start with | A sum of two numbers | *A new substance made by the reaction
test: «Cleaning products such as bleach must never be drunk, even a little, because they burn the throat.» What safe rule does this teach? | Drink a little to test how strong they are | Mix them together to make them stronger | Keep them on the kitchen table where small children can reach | *Never drink cleaning products
exam: In «the product of 7 and 8 is 56», what does product mean? | A cleaning product | The sum of 7 and 8 | *The answer when you multiply 7 and 8 | A label on a box
